UID:2224-1786647600-1786653000@lancasterbirdclub.org
SUMMARY:Monthly Club Meeting – “Osprey: Pennsylvania’s Less Appreciated Recovery Success”
DESCRIPTION:Club Meeting – Middle Creek Wildlife Management Area Visitor Center\, 100 Museum Road\, Stevens\, PA 17578 \nPresented by: Patti Barber\, Pennsylvania Game Commission  \nOsprey are an incredible success story\, but often overshowed by the recovery of bald eagles and peregrine falcons. We will cover the history of the osprey population in Pennsylvania and reasons for its decline then recovery. We will describe current monitoring efforts\, successes\, challenges\, and failures. Including the current population and distribution in the state. \nPatti Barber has studied birds on four continents\, she did her master’s research on mate guarding and paternity in red-faced warblers. She is currently the endangered bird specialist with the Pennsylvania Game Commission where she is responsible for the 20 Threatened and Endangered native birds of the state.
URL:https://lancasterbirdclub.org/event/monthly-club-meeting-unconfusing-fall-warblers-a-practical-birding-program-to-prepare-you-for-fall-migration/
LOCATION:Middle Creek Wildlife Management Area Visitor Center\, 100 Museum Road\, Stevens\, PA\, 17578\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://lancasterbirdclub.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/IMG_0926.jpeg
END:VEVENT
