SUMMARY:Beginner Birder Trip at East Lampeter Township Community Park
DESCRIPTION:Sarah Gotwols will lead an afternoon fall migration beginner birder walk at East Lampeter Township Community Park \n\nCelebrate the beauty of fall and the magic of migration with us on a beginner birding program at East Lampeter Township Community Park! Led by an expert from the Lancaster County Bird Club\, this walk is perfect for all ages—whether you’re just getting started or want to sharpen your birding skills.\n\n\n\n When: Sunday\, September 13\, 4–6 p.m.\n Where: East Lampeter Township Community Park (meet at the Lions Pavilion)\n Register to attend: https://eastlampetertownship.org/departments/parks/#birdwalk\n\nLearn how to use binoculars\, field guides\, and birding apps—and keep your eyes peeled for a variety of resident and migrating birds on their fall journey. Please bring binoculars if you have them; a limited number will be available to borrow.\n\n\n In case of bad weather\, cancellations will be announced the day before and registered participants will be notified.\n\n\n\nPresented in partnership with the Lancaster County Bird Club and East Lampeter Township Recreation.
URL:https://lancasterbirdclub.org/event/beginner-birder-trip-at-east-lampeter-township-community-park/
LOCATION:PA
CATEGORIES:Beginner Birder Trips
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://lancasterbirdclub.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/IMG_0572.jpeg
END:VEVENT
